IMPORT prelude

-- Land Transport Authority of Singapore Act 1995 (Singapore) -- the rules a member of the public meets: compensation claims for
-- railway, cross-border railway and road-tunnel works (ss 19, 20, 22, 22A, 23, 25(3) and the Fourth Schedule), outsourced
-- enforcement officers (ss 11, 11A, 11B), the Authority's enforcement powers and the obstruction offence (s 39(1)(c), (6)),
-- personal immunity (s 10), secrecy (s 41) and the Authority's symbol (s 42).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LTASA1995.txt ("version in
-- force from 23/9/2026"), with amendments to Act 5 of 2026 and S 664/2026 (wef 23/09/2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions with decision content
-- for claimants, the public and enforcement officers. Not encoded: the Authority's constitution, functions and powers (ss 3-9,
-- First Schedule), the revenue account and funds (Part 5, Second Schedule), the Compensation Board's constitution and review
-- powers (ss 26-31), transfers of staff and assets (Part 8), electronic service (ss 43, 43A), the list of specified Acts (Fifth
-- Schedule) beyond its role in s 39, the claim particulars of s 23(1), and the amount of any compensation.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Transport Authority of Singapore Act 1995 -- claims and offences`

§§ `19, 20 -- no remedy except the statutory right to compensation`

-- s 19(1): "No action, claim or proceedings shall lie or be brought against the Authority or any other person" to restrain anything
-- authorised under the Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995 or the Cross-Border Railways Act 2018, or to recover damages for loss of
-- land, chattel, trade or business, personal disturbance or inconvenience, or restriction of rights, arising from what is so
-- authorised, "except pursuant to one of the rights to compensation provided for in section 20". s 19(2): the same for ss 9, 12
-- and 29 of the Street Works Act 1995 and road-tunnel construction.
GIVEN `the act was authorised under the railway or street works provisions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the claim is made under a Fourth Schedule item` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a claim for the loss may be brought` IF
        (NOT `the act was authorised under the railway or street works provisions`)
    OR  `the claim is made under a Fourth Schedule item`

§§ `Fourth Schedule Part 1 -- items and claim periods`

-- The Part 1 table in the deposit is column-shifted; the periods below are matched to items by order and wording.
-- 1(a) displacement from an exercise of RTSA s 5 / Street Works s 9 / CBRA s 8: "Before the end of 2 years from the date on which
--      the notice is issued".
-- 1(b) other damage to land or building from the same powers: "Before the end of 6 years starting from the date on which the
--      railway ... is opened or re-opened for use by the public".
-- 2(a) structural damage from construction or operation of the railway or a road tunnel: "Before the end of 6 years from the date
--      of the opening for public traffic"; 2(b) displacement from that damage: "Same as in item (a) above".
-- 3    damage from works under RTSA s 9 (and equivalents): "Before the end of one year from the date of completion of the work".
-- 4    cost of altering apparatus and repairing street surface: "Before the end of one year from the completion of the alteration
--      and repair".
-- 5(a) cost of removing a lawful object or structure: one year "from the date of removal"; 5(b) reinstating or replacing it: one
--      year "from the date of reinstatement or replacement"; 5(c) loss where it is not reinstated: one year "from the date of
--      removal".
DECLARE ClaimItem IS ONE OF
    `1(a) displacement under a temporary possession notice`
    `1(b) other damage from temporary possession`
    `2(a) structural damage from the railway or a road tunnel`
    `2(b) displacement from structural damage`
    `3 damage from works on land`
    `4 cost of altering apparatus and street surface`
    `5(a) cost of removing an object or structure`
    `5(b) cost of reinstating an object or structure`
    `5(c) loss of an object or structure not reinstated`

GIVEN `the item` IS A ClaimItem
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claim period in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `1(a) displacement under a temporary possession notice` THEN 2
    WHEN `1(b) other damage from temporary possession` THEN 6
    WHEN `2(a) structural damage from the railway or a road tunnel` THEN 6
    WHEN `2(b) displacement from structural damage` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 1

§§ `22 -- claims out of time`

-- s 22(1): a claim not served "before the end of the period specified in the fourth column" is barred.
-- (4): the Compensation Board MAY extend the period if (a) the delay "was occasioned by mistake of fact or mistake of any matter of
-- law (other than the relevant provision in the fourth column of Part 1 of the Fourth Schedule) or by any other reasonable cause";
-- OR (b) "the Authority is not materially affected in the conduct of its case or otherwise by the delay".
-- (5): "not in any case exceeding 6 years from the time when the right to compensation first arose".
-- A mistake about the claim period itself is not a qualifying mistake; whether it could still be "any other reasonable cause" is not
-- decided here -- the encoding treats it as not qualifying under (a) (an inference).
GIVEN `the delay was caused by a mistake of fact or law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the mistake was about the claim period itself` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the delay had some other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Authority is not materially affected by the delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may extend the claim period` IF
        (`the delay was caused by a mistake of fact or law` AND (NOT `the mistake was about the claim period itself`))
    OR  `the delay had some other reasonable cause`
    OR  `the Authority is not materially affected by the delay`

-- Times are in years. "Before the end of" a period of N years is read as strictly less than N years after its start.
-- An extension, if granted, is expressed as the number of years after the right first arose by which the claim must be served;
-- 0 means no extension.
GIVEN `the item` IS A ClaimItem,
      `years from the start of the period to service` IS A NUMBER,
      `years from the right arising to service` IS A NUMBER,
      `extended to years after the right arose` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is in time` IF
        `years from the start of the period to service` LESS THAN `the claim period in years` `the item`
    OR  (    `extended to years after the right arose` GREATER THAN 0
         AND `extended to years after the right arose` AT MOST 6
         AND `years from the right arising to service` AT MOST `extended to years after the right arose`)

§§ `22A -- owners who served a notice under the possession provisions`

-- s 22A(1)-(3): an owner whose land was temporarily possessed (RTSA s 5, CBRA s 8, Street Works s 9) and who gives the Authority the
-- notice under RTSA s 7(1) (or the equivalents) within the claim period "is entitled to claim only for loss due to displacement of
-- any person in lawful occupation of the land ... and no other item in the Fourth Schedule". Identifying that loss with item 1(a)
-- is an inference.
GIVEN `the item` IS A ClaimItem, `the owner gave the possession notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may claim the item` IF
    IF `the owner gave the possession notice`
    THEN CONSIDER `the item`
         WHEN `1(a) displacement under a temporary possession notice` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `23 -- claims procedure`

-- s 23(3): if a claimant amends a claim before Board proceedings and the Authority considers the amendment substantial, it may,
-- "within 14 days of the receipt of the amended claim", elect to treat it as a new claim.
GIVEN `Board proceedings have begun` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amendment is substantial` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since the amended claim was received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may treat the amended claim as new` IF
    (NOT `Board proceedings have begun`) AND `the amendment is substantial` AND `days since the amended claim was received` AT MOST 14

-- s 23(4): if requested particulars "are not supplied ... within a period of 28 days from the date of the notice, or within any
-- further period that the Authority may in writing allow, the claim or the item ... is deemed to be rejected". Reading the further
-- period as added to the 28 days is an inference.
GIVEN `particulars were requested` IS A BOOLEAN, `particulars were supplied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since the request` IS A NUMBER, `further days allowed in writing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is deemed rejected` IF
        `particulars were requested`
    AND (NOT `particulars were supplied`)
    AND `days since the request` GREATER THAN (28 PLUS `further days allowed in writing`)

-- s 23(5): the Authority must answer (admit, reject, or part) "within 3 months of the service of a claim".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months for the Authority to answer a claim` MEANS 3

-- s 23(8): "If, at the end of 4 months from the receipt of a claim by the Authority, it has not been settled by agreement, either
-- the claimant or the Authority may commence proceedings before the Compensation Board".
GIVEN `months since the claim was received` IS A NUMBER, `the claim has been settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `either side may go to the Compensation Board` IF
    `months since the claim was received` AT LEAST 4 AND (NOT `the claim has been settled`)

§§ `25(3) -- refusing an offer`

-- s 25(3): where an offer is refused and the compensation including costs assessed by the Board "does not exceed" the offer, the
-- Board "must, unless for special reasons the Board thinks it proper not to do so, order the party who refused the offer to bear the
-- party's own costs and to pay the costs of the other party" incurred after the offer.
GIVEN `the offer was refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount assessed` IS A NUMBER, `the amount offered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Board finds special reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusing party pays the costs after the offer` IF
    `the offer was refused` AND `the amount assessed` AT MOST `the amount offered` AND (NOT `the Board finds special reasons`)

§§ `Fourth Schedule Part 2 -- assessing compensation`

-- para 2: "compensatable interest" means (a) an unexpired term "of not less than one month" or a tenancy terminable "by giving not
-- less than one month's notice"; (b) a mortgagee in possession; (c) the holder of a valid option to purchase such an interest;
-- (d) a purchaser to whom the benefit has passed.
DECLARE Interest IS ONE OF
    `an owner or lessee with an unexpired term`
    `a tenant on periodic notice`
    `a mortgagee in possession`
    `a mortgagee not in possession`
    `an option holder`
    `a purchaser to whom the benefit has passed`
    `a licensee`

GIVEN `the interest` IS A Interest, `months of term or notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is compensatable` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`
    WHEN `an owner or lessee with an unexpired term` THEN `months of term or notice` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `a tenant on periodic notice` THEN `months of term or notice` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `a mortgagee in possession` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an option holder` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a purchaser to whom the benefit has passed` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- para 3: "no account is to be taken of (a) the financial loss resulting from the interruption of or interference with any trade or
-- business carried on any land; and (b) any increase or decrease in the value of land ... attributable to" the delineation of the
-- railway area or "the construction or operation of any railway or road".
-- para 6: no compensation under item 5(c) for the lost benefit of advertising on a removed sign.
DECLARE Head IS ONE OF
    `cost of repairing the damage`
    `cost of moving to alternative premises`
    `loss of trade from the works`
    `fall in land value from the railway`
    `rise in land value from the railway`
    `lost advertising benefit of a removed sign`

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the head counts in the assessment` IF
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `cost of repairing the damage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cost of moving to alternative premises` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `11, 11A -- outsourced enforcement officers`

-- s 11(1): the Authority may appoint an individual who "(a) is at least 18 years of age; (b) is not an employee of the Authority;
-- (c) is not a public officer; and (d) has suitable qualifications or experience".
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `is an employee of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has suitable qualifications or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed an outsourced enforcement officer` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 18
    AND (NOT `is an employee of the Authority`)
    AND (NOT `is a public officer`)
    AND `has suitable qualifications or experience`

-- s 11A(3): "the Chief Executive cannot authorise under this section an outsourced enforcement officer to arrest any individual".
-- (4): powers may be exercised only "(a) when in uniform, and upon production of the identification card ...; (b) to the extent
-- authorised ...; and (c) as directed (generally or specially) by an officer or employee of the Authority". (7): direction does not
-- lapse "by reason only that the officer or employee of the Authority is not present".
GIVEN `the power is arrest` IS A BOOLEAN, `in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `produced the identification card` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `within the written authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed by an Authority officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the outsourced officer may exercise the power` IF
        (NOT `the power is arrest`)
    AND `in uniform`
    AND `produced the identification card`
    AND `within the written authorisation`
    AND `directed by an Authority officer`

-- s 39(1)(c): by contrast an officer or employee of the Authority "if he or she is generally or specially authorised in writing by
-- the Chief Executive", may "arrest without warrant" a person found committing an offence under a Fifth Schedule law. The
-- declaration of office and production of the identification card in s 39(1) opening words are required.
GIVEN `authorised in writing by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared office and produced the card` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `offence under a specified Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Authority officer may arrest without warrant` IF
    `authorised in writing by the Chief Executive` AND `declared office and produced the card` AND `offence under a specified Act`

§§ `11B -- impersonation and misuse`

-- s 11B(1): an individual who represents himself or herself "by word or conduct to be an outsourced enforcement officer when he or
-- she is not" commits an offence. (2): an outsourced enforcement officer who uses issued accoutrement, equipment or identification
-- card "otherwise than in the course of, or for the purpose of, exercising the functions" commits an offence. Both: $2,500 or
-- 6 months or both. (3): "it is a defence ... where the accused proves, on a balance of probabilities" use or possession "for the
-- purposes of a public entertainment provided in compliance with the Public Entertainments Act 1958".
GIVEN `represented being an outsourced enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an outsourced enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved use for a lawful public entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `impersonation is an offence` IF
        `represented being an outsourced enforcement officer`
    AND (NOT `is an outsourced enforcement officer`)
    AND (NOT `proved use for a lawful public entertainment`)

GIVEN `is an outsourced enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `used the issued kit or card` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the course of the officer's functions` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved use for a lawful public entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `misuse of issued kit is an offence` IF
        `is an outsourced enforcement officer`
    AND `used the issued kit or card`
    AND (NOT `in the course of the officer's functions`)
    AND (NOT `proved use for a lawful public entertainment`)

§§ `39(6) -- obstructing the Authority`

-- s 39(6): a person who "(a) refuses to give access to, or assaults, obstructs, hinders or delays" an officer; "(b) wilfully
-- misstates or without lawful excuse refuses to give any information, or without lawful excuse refuses to produce any book,
-- document"; or "(c) fails to comply with a lawful demand" -- $5,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `obstructed or refused access` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully misstated information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `refused information or documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a lawful excuse for the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `failed to comply with a lawful demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obstructing the Authority is an offence` IF
        `obstructed or refused access`
    OR  `wilfully misstated information`
    OR  (`refused information or documents` AND (NOT `had a lawful excuse for the refusal`))
    OR  `failed to comply with a lawful demand`

§§ `10 -- personal immunity`

-- s 10: "No liability shall lie personally against any member, officer or employee of the Authority or any other person acting under
-- the direction of the Authority for anything done or intended to be done in good faith and with reasonable care".
GIVEN `acting for or under the direction of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is personally immune` IF
    `acting for or under the direction of the Authority` AND `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care`

§§ `41, 42 -- secrecy and the Authority's symbol`

-- s 41(1): a person who "is or has been" a member, officer, employee or agent of the Authority or a committee member must not
-- disclose information obtained in the performance of duties, "Except for the purpose of the performance of duties or the exercise
-- of functions or when lawfully required to do so by any court or where required or allowed by the provisions of any written law".
-- (2): $2,000 or one year or both.
GIVEN `is or was an insider of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained the information in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `is or was an insider of the Authority`
    AND `obtained the information in the course of duties`
    AND (NOT `disclosed in performing duties`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

-- s 42(2): "Any person who uses a symbol or representation identical with that of the Authority, or which so resembles [it] as to
-- deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" -- $2,000 or 6 months or both. No exception for
-- the Authority's licensees appears in the section.
GIVEN `identical to the Authority's symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
    `identical to the Authority's symbol` OR `likely to deceive or confuse`

§§ `Penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `impersonating an outsourced enforcement officer`
    `misusing issued kit`
    `obstructing the Authority`
    `breaching secrecy`
    `using the Authority's symbol`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `impersonating an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN 2500
    WHEN `misusing issued kit` THEN 2500
    WHEN `obstructing the Authority` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing the Authority` THEN 12
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6
